MCQS_CAT6 = r"""
    <!-- ═══════════ 6.x: Advanced Cluster Mesh (Q157–Q168) ═══════════ -->
    <div class="section-block" id="cat6-adv"><h3>Advanced Cluster Mesh (Q157–Q168)</h3>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q157" data-correct="C"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q157 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh service affinity modes?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Only random</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Only local preferred</div><div class="mcq-option">C) "local" (prefer local cluster backends, fail to remote), "remote" (prefer remote), "none" (no preference, round-robin across all clusters). Set via annotation: io.cilium/service-affinity</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Always local cluster first</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a157')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a157"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: C</div><p>Annotation: `io.cilium/service-affinity: local`. Use local for low latency, remote for active/passive DR, none for true global load balancing.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q158" data-correct="A"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q158 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh etcd — deployment options?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) External etcd (separate HA cluster, production recommended) OR embedded etcd (cilium clustermesh enable creates internal etcd via StatefulSet). External: managed etcd, K8s etcd, or dedicated cluster</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Only external etcd</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Only embedded etcd</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Uses K8s API server instead of etcd</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a158')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a158"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: A</div><p>External etcd: `--set clustermesh.apiserver.etcd.endpoints=etcd-cluster:2379`. Embedded: simpler for testing. Production: external HA etcd (3+ nodes).</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q159" data-correct="B"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q159 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cross-cluster NetworkPolicy in Cluster Mesh?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Not supported — policies are cluster-local</div><div class="mcq-option">B) CiliumNetworkPolicy can use `fromEntities: [cluster]` for remote clusters. Global identities shared via etcd. Policies referencing labels work across clusters automatically</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Only allow-all between clusters</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Requires separate cross-cluster policy CRD</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a159')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a159"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: B</div><p>Since identities are global (identity@cluster-id), a CNP in cluster-1 can allow/deny traffic from cluster-2 pods. `fromEntities: [cluster]` applies to all clusters.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q160" data-correct="D"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q160 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh pod CIDR overlap — what happens?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Auto-detects and renumbers</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Works fine — identities handle it</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Only egress works, no ingress</div><div class="mcq-option">D) BREAKS routing — overlapping CIDRs cause wrong routing decisions. Pod IPs must be unique across all clusters. Solution: re-IP or use identity-based routing (future)</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a160')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a160"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: D</div><p>This is why the requirement says "non-overlapping pod CIDRs." If 10.0.0.5 exists in both clusters, routing is ambiguous. Identity doesn't fix IP routing.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q161" data-correct="A"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q161 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">cilium clustermesh status — what does it show?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Connected clusters list, their cluster IDs, last heartbeat, shared services count, identities sync status. Shows healthy/down per cluster. Critical for troubleshooting</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Only peer IP addresses</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Same as cilium status</div><div class="mcq-option">D) BGP peer status</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a161')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a161"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: A</div><p>Example output: Cluster-2 (ID:2): ready, 156 identities, 12 shared services, last heartbeat 3s ago. If "down" — check TLS, etcd, network.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q162" data-correct="C"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q162 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Multi-cluster service — how to create?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Automatic for all services</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Special CRD only</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Annotate Service: `io.cilium/global-service: "true"`. The service becomes available in all connected clusters with same ClusterIP. Backends from all clusters aggregated</div><div class="mcq-option">D) kubectl expose with --cluster-mesh flag</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a162')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a162"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: C</div><p>Just add the annotation. If service exists in multiple clusters, backends merged. `cilium service list` shows backends with cluster ID prefix.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q163" data-correct="B"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q163 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Egress Gateway policy — how to define?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Only via Helm values</div><div class="mcq-option">B) CiliumEgressGatewayPolicy CRD: select pods via podSelector, specify destination CIDRs, egress IP. Gateway nodes selected via nodeSelector. Traffic exits from gateway node with fixed IP</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Via CiliumNetworkPolicy egress section</div><div class="mcq-option">D) kubectl annotate pod</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a163')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a163"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: B</div><p>CRD defines: which pods → which destinations → which egress IP → which gateway nodes. Multiple policies can share same gateway. Gateway selection via node labels.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q164" data-correct="A"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q164 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh: split-brain scenario?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) If etcd connectivity lost between clusters, each cluster operates independently with LOCAL backends. When connectivity restores, identities re-sync. No split-brain in data plane — each cluster uses its own etcd</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Both clusters stop working</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Random traffic drops</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Automatic leader election resolves</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a164')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a164"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: A</div><p>Each cluster has its own etcd for local state. Cluster Mesh etcd is for identity+service sync only. During partition: local services continue. Remote backends unreachable until connectivity restores.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q165" data-correct="C"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q165 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cross-cluster observability with Hubble?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Not possible — Hubble is per-cluster</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Hubble auto-merges all clusters</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Each cluster has its own Hubble Relay + UI. For unified view: aggregate metrics in central Prometheus/Thanos. Hubble CLI can switch contexts to query different clusters</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Only via Cilium CLI</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a165')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a165"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: C</div><p>Hubble is cluster-scoped. For global visibility: Thanos/Cortex for metrics, Grafana with multi-cluster dashboards. Hubble CLI: `hubble observe --context cluster-1`.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q166" data-correct="D"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q166 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh vs Service Mesh (Istio/Linkerd)?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) Same thing — different name</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Cluster Mesh replaces Service Mesh</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Service Mesh replaces Cluster Mesh</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Different layers: Cluster Mesh = L3/L4 multi-cluster networking (IP reachability, routing, identities). Service Mesh = L7 traffic management (retries, timeouts, mTLS, canary). They COMPLEMENT each other — Cilium + Istio is a common pattern</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a166')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a166"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: D</div><p>Cluster Mesh handles HOW pods reach each other across clusters. Service Mesh handles WHAT happens to requests (retries, circuit breaking, tracing). Use together for complete multi-cluster.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q167" data-correct="B"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q167 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh bandwidth requirements?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) No specific requirements</div><div class="mcq-option">B) etcd sync: minimal (KB/s for identity/service updates). Data plane: depends on cross-cluster pod traffic. Recommendation: minimum 10 Mbps between clusters for control plane stability. Latency < 100ms for identity sync</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Only 1 Gbps minimum</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Bandwidth doesn't matter — only latency</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a167')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a167"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: B</div><p>Control plane: lightweight identity sync via etcd watchers. Data plane: whatever your cross-cluster apps need. High latency (>100ms) can slow identity propagation and cause policy delays.</p></div></div>

    <div class="mcq-block" id="q168" data-correct="A"><div class="mcq-number"><span class="domain-pill d6">Cluster Mesh</span> Q168 of 200</div><div class="mcq-question">Cluster Mesh with overlapping services?</div><div class="mcq-options"><div class="mcq-option">A) If same service name exists in multiple clusters, annotating ALL with `global-service: true` MERGES their backends. If only one annotated, that cluster's backends are the global backends. Use service affinity to control routing</div><div class="mcq-option">B) Overlapping services cause errors</div><div class="mcq-option">C) Only one cluster's service wins</div><div class="mcq-option">D) Services must have different names</div></div><button class="mcq-toggle-btn" onclick="toggleAnswer('a168')">👁️ Show Answer &amp; Explanation</button><div class="mcq-answer" id="a168"><div class="answer-label">✅ Correct Answer: A</div><p>Same name + same namespace + global annotation = merged. Pod backends from all clusters. Cilium internally prepends cluster-id to differentiate identical pod IPs.</p></div></div>
    </div>
"""

